# Browser-Only Policy (No PWA / Not Installable)

The marketing and documentation website (`my-app`) is explicitly designed and required to behave strictly as a public, browser-accessible website, NOT an installable Progressive Web App.

## Invariant Rules

- **Manifest `display: "browser"` (CRITICAL)**: `src/app/manifest.ts` MUST always keep `display: 'browser'`. NEVER change it to `standalone`, `minimal-ui`, or `fullscreen`.
- **Zero Service Workers**: NEVER add a service worker, `next-pwa`, Workbox, offline caching, or background sync scripts to `my-app`.
- **No Install Prompts or Banners**: NEVER add `beforeinstallprompt` event listeners, "Add to Home Screen" buttons, or PWA install modal prompts.
- **Brand Signals Only**: The `manifest.ts` file exists solely for search engine identity and browser tab icon metadata (name, description, theme color, icons).
- **Scope Distinction**: This restriction applies strictly to `my-app`. The merchant tenant portal (`tenant-portal`) is a separate app with its own PWA capabilities.

## ❌ FORBIDDEN vs ✅ REQUIRED

### 1. Web App Manifest Display Mode

```typescript
// ❌ FORBIDDEN — Standalone mode triggering Chrome install heuristics
// src/app/manifest.ts
export default function manifest(): MetadataRoute.Manifest {
  return {
    name: 'Cashvio',
    display: 'standalone', // FORBIDDEN!
    start_url: '/',
  };
}

// ✅ REQUIRED — Browser display mode keeping site strictly web-only
// src/app/manifest.ts
export default function manifest(): MetadataRoute.Manifest {
  return {
    name: 'Cashvio',
    short_name: 'Cashvio',
    description: 'Free POS & Online Store Platform',
    start_url: '/',
    display: 'browser', // Intentional and required
    background_color: '#faf9f7',
    theme_color: '#059669',
    icons: [
      { src: '/icon-192.png', sizes: '192x192', type: 'image/png' },
      { src: '/icon-512.png', sizes: '512x512', type: 'image/png' },
    ],
  };
}
```

### 2. Service Worker Registration

```tsx
// ❌ FORBIDDEN — Service worker registration in client layout/component
useEffect(() => {
  if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
    navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js');
  }
}, []);

// ✅ REQUIRED — No service worker registration code anywhere in the codebase.
```
